{"name":"Whippet","hex":"#cec1b5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whippet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dog of a certain breed, similar to a small greyhound, originating in Britain and bred for racing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cartridge of nitrous oxide (laughing gas), used as a recreational inhalant drug."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whippet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whippet","blocks":[{"text":"The Whippet is a British breed of sighthound. It closely resembles the Greyhound and the smaller Italian Greyhound, and is intermediate between them in size. In the nineteenth century, it was sometimes called \"the poor man's racehorse\". It is commonly kept as a companion dog, for competitive showing or for amateur racing, and may participate in various dog sports, including lure coursing, agility, and flyball. It has the fastest running speed within its weight and size range, and is believed to have the fastest idle-to-running acceleration of any dog."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Whippet_2018_6.jpg/330px-Whippet_2018_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whippet"},{"title":"Whippet (bus company)","blocks":[{"text":"Whippet is a bus and coach operator based in Swavesey, Cambridgeshire, England. It is part of the Ascendal Group."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/%28GBR-Cambridgeshire%29_Whippet_Coaches_WG114_MX23LCW_U1_2023-11-17.jpg/330px-%28GBR-Cambridgeshire%29_Whippet_Coaches_WG114_MX23LCW_U1_2023-11-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whippet_(bus_company)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Misse_and_Turlu%2C_Two_Greyhounds_Belonging_to_Louis_XV.jpg/500px-Misse_and_Turlu%2C_Two_Greyhounds_Belonging_to_Louis_XV.jpg?utm_source=en.wi